        "locator_id": "WEB01-E03",
        "corpus_chunk": null,
        "section": "Abstract (PubMed)",
        "passage_type": "faithful_paraphrase",
        "text": "Co\u2011contaminants benzene (0.5\u20134.8 mg/L) and trichloroethylene (0.5\u20138 mg/L) reduced PFOS adsorption by roughly twenty\u2011fold at the highest TCE level, while effects on PFOA were neutral to slightly promotive, highlighting PFAS\u2011specific competitive effects."
